{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["יעור פקחים — with regard to one who sees, the term blindness is apt. And with regard to צדיק, it is a substitution."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "Rashbam explains that the root עור, normally 'blind,' is used here figuratively: it fits naturally with פקחים (those who can see) but is a forced substitution with צדיק. The word סילוף means a distorting or substituting of the normal sense."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:42:47.691351979Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}